    <item>
      <title>Revisão nas provas da LPIC-2 e LPIC-3</title>
      <link>http://localhost:1313/revisao-nas-provas-da-lpic-2-e-lpic-3/</link>
      <pubDate>Thu, 24 Jan 2013 00:00:00 +0000</pubDate>
      <author>eurodrigolira@gmail.com (Rodrigo Lira)</author>
      <guid>http://localhost:1313/revisao-nas-provas-da-lpic-2-e-lpic-3/</guid>
      <description>&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href=&#34;http://rodrigolira.eti.br/wp-content/uploads/2013/01/lpi.jpg&#34;  target=&#34;_blank&#34; rel=&#34;noreferrer&#34;&gt;&lt;figure&gt;&lt;img&#xA;    class=&#34;my-0 rounded-md&#34;&#xA;    loading=&#34;lazy&#34;&#xA;    decoding=&#34;async&#34;&#xA;    fetchpriority=&#34;auto&#34;&#xA;    alt=&#34;&#34;&#xA;    width=&#34;194&#34;&#xA;    height=&#34;300&#34;&#xA;    src=&#34;http://localhost:1313/revisao-nas-provas-da-lpic-2-e-lpic-3/images/lpi-194x300.jpg&#34;&#xA;    srcset=&#34;http://localhost:1313/revisao-nas-provas-da-lpic-2-e-lpic-3/images/lpi-194x300.jpg 800w, http://localhost:1313/revisao-nas-provas-da-lpic-2-e-lpic-3/images/lpi-194x300.jpg 1280w&#34;&#xA;    sizes=&#34;(min-width: 768px) 50vw, 65vw&#34;&#xA;    data-zoom-src=&#34;http://localhost:1313/revisao-nas-provas-da-lpic-2-e-lpic-3/images/lpi-194x300.jpg&#34;&gt;&lt;figcaption&gt;lpi&lt;/figcaption&gt;&lt;/figure&gt;&#xA;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;A LPI (Linux Professional Institute) anunciou hoje que novas mudanças para seu programa de certificação LPIC-2 e LPIC-3. Segue a baixo a noticia.&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;(Sacramento, CA, USA: January 24, 2013) The Linux Professional Institute (LPI), the world&amp;rsquo;s premier Linux certification organization, announced upcoming changes to their LPIC-2 and LPIC-3 certification programs. New objectives for these certifications are presently under development. New exams will be available in English on October 1, 2013 with local translations and pricing TBA.&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;&amp;ldquo;Following extensive consultations with partner organizations and industry representatives we will be concentrating essential and advanced system administration skills in LPIC-2 while further focusing the LPIC-3 program on specific specialties: Mixed Environments, Security, and High Availability/Virtualization, &amp;quot; said Jim Lacey, President and CEO of the Linux Professional Institute. Mr. Lacey added that these upcoming changes also reflect LPI&amp;rsquo;s engagement with the wider Open Source community in determining the best skill sets required for a variety of specialized job roles for Linux professionals.&lt;/p&gt;</description>
      
    </item>
    
